To check if ransomNote can be constructed using letters from magazine, you can iterate through each character in ransomNote and check if it exists in magazine. If it does, remove that character from magazine so it cannot be used again. If all characters in ransomNote can be found in magazine and use each character of magazine only once, return true. Otherwise, return false.

Here's the Python code that implements this logic:
```
def can_construct(ransomNote, magazine):
    char_count = {}
    for char in magazine:
        if char not in char_count:
            char_count[char] = 1
        else:
            char_count[char] += 1

    for char in ransomNote:
        if char not in char_count or char_count[char] == 0:
            return False
        else:
            char_count[char] -= 1

    return True
``` 

